commit(n,t,ds,ch,items,'Landscape sheet, already upright in the supplied image. Two general diamonds and an indexed diamond compare unreduced and normalized complexes; the lower diamond is dual. Stars and bullets, bracketed indices and parentheses have different roles. The upper second degree case visibly has n,n-1, correcting C’s plus, while its heavily overwritten left subscript m/n remains uncertain. The lower degree parenthesis has an unresolved small plus/minus and is not silently harmonized. The right diamond’s lower-left isomorphism label reads n>=m+1, not H’s <=. The text retains the unbracketed C_(m+1)^m in the second alors display even though its value k^(m+2) belongs to the unnormalized exterior-power term; H inserts brackets. The chain inclusion visibly has Cbb_a(X_bullet), where the preceding setup would suggest Cbb_*(X_*); the oval and round dot are kept. The upper marginal Hom! definition states that the image equals Delta^n (i.e surj) or [0,n-1], not H’s negative containment phrase. The author qualifies the diagonal-injection remark with sans doute. Foot number 339.',hand=['A true star has crossing arms, while the bullet is a round filled mark. In the chain inclusion the RHS argument has a dot even though the LHS has a star; no normalization was made.','Square brackets [m] are distinct from rounded (m), especially in the indexed diamond and the upper component definitions. H alternates or supplies brackets differently.','The doubled C denotes unreduced objects in the surrounding notation; the simple C marks normalized exterior-power objects. Faint retracing can obscure the distinction, so the local contrast and the object’s repeated notation were checked together.','Only the phrase et iso can. is crossed under the lower-right arrow; a strike near an arrow is not cancellation of every label above it.'],notation=[('Cbb versus C','Doubled and single C are distinguished in the two diamonds and exterior-power descriptions.'),('star / bullet','Starred simplicial/cosimplicial objects versus bullet-indexed complexes; clear written exceptions retained.'),('Hom!','Increasing maps whose image is Delta^n or [0,n-1], as explicitly defined on this sheet.'),('ND','Capital N and D in the normalization identification.')],abbr=[('ens','ensemble'),('surj','surjectif'),('iso','isomorphisme'),('fact. dir. can.','facteur direct canonique'),('deg','degré(s)')],checks=[check('338-text-complexes','Definitions, diamonds and degree claims carried as written; no normalization theorem proved here.'),check('338-degree-incidence','From the written condition C_n^m nonzero only for n=m or m+1, solving for m at fixed n gives m=n or n-1. This led to checking the upper minus against the ink.','targeted proof check'),check('338-text-diagonal','The author says sans doute for the diagonal injection; this run does not promote that assertion to a verified theorem.')],unresolved=[r'upper left subscript m|n',r'pale on a',r'lower degree plus/minus',r'unit word unité|mixte',r'cancelled Hom and final k'])
